# Honey Garlic Chicken

Based on [Family Food on the Table](https://www.familyfoodonthetable.com/15-minute-honey-garlic-chicken) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251224030622/https://www.familyfoodonthetable.com/15-minute-honey-garlic-chicken/))

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 2 teaspoons [extra-virgin olive oil]{ ing="extra-virgin-olive-oil" } (or canola oil)
- [ ] 1½ pounds [boneless, skinless chicken breasts]{ ing="boneless-skinless-chicken-breasts" }, cut into ½-inch cubes
- [ ] [Salt and black pepper]{ ing="salt-and-black-pepper" }
- [ ] 3 tablespoons [honey]{ ing="honey" }
- [ ] 3 tablespoons [low-sodium soy sauce]{ ing="low-sodium-soy-sauce" }
- [ ] 3 cloves [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, minced
- [ ] ¼ teaspoon [red pepper flakes]{ ing="red-pepper-flakes" } (optional, omit for young kids)

### For Serving

- [ ] [Steamed brown]{ ing="steamed-brown" } or white rice
- [ ] [Green onions]{ ing="green-onions" }, sliced
- [ ] [Sesame seeds]{ ing="sesame-seeds" }
- [ ] [Peanuts]{ ing="peanuts" }
- [ ] [Lime wedges]{ ing="lime-wedges" }

## Recipe

1. Heat [olive oil]{ ing="extra-virgin-olive-oil" } in a large skillet over medium-high heat
1. Season cubed chicken lightly with salt and [pepper]{ ing="salt-and-black-pepper" } (go light on salt since [soy sauce]{ ing="low-sodium-soy-sauce" } adds sodium)
1. Add chicken to hot skillet and cook without stirring for 3-4 minutes to [brown]{ ing="steamed-brown" } one side
1. While chicken [browns]{ ing="steamed-brown" }, whisk together [honey]{ ing="honey" }, [soy sauce]{ ing="low-sodium-soy-sauce" }, minced [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, and [red pepper flakes]{ ing="red-pepper-flakes" } (if using) in a small bowl
1. Flip chicken pieces and immediately add the [honey]{ ing="honey" } [garlic]{ ing="garlic" } [sauce]{ ing="low-sodium-soy-sauce" } to the pan
1. Toss chicken to coat evenly in [sauce]{ ing="low-sodium-soy-sauce" } and cook 4-5 more minutes until chicken is fully cooked through (internal temperature 165°F)
1. Serve immediately over steamed rice with desired toppings

## Notes

- The small chicken pieces cook quickly, so be careful not to overcook them or they’ll become dry
- For a thicker sauce, mix 1-3 teaspoons cornstarch with 1 tablespoon water and add in the final 1-2 minutes of cooking
- Many cooks recommend doubling the sauce for a more generous coating on rice and vegetables
- The sweet-savory glaze makes this particularly appealing to children, even picky eaters
- Total cook time is genuinely 15 minutes, making this perfect for busy weeknights
- Pairs well with steamed broccoli, snap peas, or stir-fried vegetables
- Store leftovers in an airtight container for up to 3 days. Reheats well in the microwave
